---
type: statement
kind: proposition
slug: light-tails-equivalence
---

<script>
  import Proof from '$lib/components/proof.svelte';
</script>

We have $\odeSpace = \vecSpace$ if and only if each $\momentVar \in \vecSpace$ is such that there exists $\tau > 0$ in which $\momentVar$ is a finite moment of the associated marginal $\X_\tau$.
$$
  \Exp_{\Prb_\stateVar}\exp\prj{\momentVar}{\X_\tau} < \infty, \quad \stateVar \in \stateSpace
$$

<Proof>

For sufficiency, first see that any $\momentVar \in \vecSpace$ is such that $\closedBall{\momentVar}{1} \subseteq \vecSpace = \odeSpace^\circ$ is compact.
By [%full](/statements/compact-ode-existence), we then have some $\tau > 0$ so that $\momentVar \in \closedBall{\momentVar}{1} \subseteq \momentSpace(\tau)$.
Then, [%full(a)](/statements/keller-ressel-mayerhofer) gives us the desired finiteness condition.
$$
  \Exp_{\Prb_\stateVar}\exp\prj{\momentVar}{\X_\tau} = \exp\aff(\tau, \momentVar, \stateVar) < \infty, \quad \stateVar \in \stateSpace
$$
Conversely, if $\momentVar \in \vecSpace$ satisfies $\Exp_{\Prb_\stateVar}\exp\prj{\momentVar}{\X_\tau} < \infty$ for all $\stateVar \in \stateSpace$, then it certainly does for some $\stateVar \in \stateSpace^\circ$, and so [%full(b)](/statements/keller-ressel-mayerhofer) gives us $(\tau, \momentVar) \in \momentSpace$.
Surely, this then means that $\momentVar \in \momentSpace(\tau) \subseteq \odeSpace$.

</Proof>
